id: k8s.volume
kind: kubernetes
title: Volume
aliases: volume, emptyDir, hostPath
tags: storage
questions:
  - what happens to data written to a container filesystem?
invariant: Container filesystems are ephemeral; anything that must outlive a container restart lives in a Volume.
answer_30s: A Volume is a directory with a lifetime tied to the Pod (or longer for persistent volumes); without one, writes are lost when the container restarts.
answer_2m: |
  Distinguish lifetimes: `emptyDir` dies with the Pod (fine for scratch and for
  sharing files between containers), `hostPath` binds a node path (couples you
  to a node, mostly for agents and debugging), ConfigMap/Secret volumes are
  read-only projections, and a PVC outlives the Pod. The last one is what makes
  a StatefulSet meaningful.
when_to_use:
  - scratch space shared between containers, or durable state via a PVC
avoid_when:
  - durable data without a PVC
related:
  - k8s.pvc
  - k8s.configmap
  - k8s.secret
sources:
  - https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/storage/volumes/
